// Title: Use of Scriptrunner.exe
// Sigma ID: 64760eef-87f7-4ed3-93fd-655668ea9420
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: The "ScriptRunner.exe" binary can be abused to proxy execution through it and bypass possible
//   whitelisting
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use when App-v is deployed
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Scriptrunner/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_scriptrunner.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ScriptRunner.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ScriptRunner.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " -appvscript "
